/-!
# Base change of a quasi-regular immersion

Let `i : Z ⟶ X` be an immersion of schemes over a base `S` whose source is flat over `S`.  If `i`
is a quasi-regular immersion, then so is its base change along any `S' ⟶ S`.  This is the
quasi-regular half of Stacks tag 063R.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.isGeneratedByOn_definingIdealOfHom_of_ker_app_eq_span`: the converse
  of `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ker_app_eq_span_range`.  If over an affine open the kernel of
  `j.app` is the ideal generated by a family of sections, then that family generates the defining
  ideal sheaf there.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.isQuasiRegular_and_isH1Regular_of_isPushout_of_ker_eq_span`: Stacks
  tag 0CEP read off a pushout square of rings, for both the quasi-regular and the `H₁`-regular
  condition.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.isQuasiRegularIdealSheaf_definingIdealOfHom_of_isPullback`: for a
  closed immersion `j : Z ⟶ Y` of schemes over `S` with `Z ⟶ S` flat, quasi-regularity of the
  defining ideal of `j` is inherited by the defining ideal of its base change along `S' ⟶ S`.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.isQuasiRegularImmersion_of_isPullback`: the same for an arbitrary
  immersion and an arbitrary cartesian square.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.isQuasiRegularImmersion_baseChange_of_flat`: **the quasi-regular half
  of Stacks tag 063R**, in the `pullback` spelling.

## Implementation notes

The whole argument is affine-local, and the structural difficulty is that `i.coborderRange` does
*not* commute with base change: the range of an immersion commutes with preimage but its coborder
does not.  That difficulty is settled elsewhere, by part (4) of Stacks tag 063J
(`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.isQuasiRegularImmersion_iff_of_open`) and its corollary
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.isQuasiRegularImmersion_baseChange_iff`, which says that the base change
of an immersion is quasi-regular exactly when the defining ideal of
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.baseChangeLiftCoborder` on `p ⁻¹ᵁ i.coborderRange` is quasi-regular.  So
no coborder reasoning appears here; what is left is a statement about the defining ideal of a
closed immersion on one named open, and that is the theorem proved for closed immersions and
transported.

For a closed immersion the affine-local argument is this.  Near a point of the base-changed
subscheme choose an affine open `V` of `S`, an affine open `U` of `Y` over `V` on which the
defining ideal of `j` is generated by a quasi-regular family `s` (Stacks tag 063G), an affine open
`W` of `S'` over `V`, and the affine open `U' = a⁻¹U ⊓ h'⁻¹W` of `Y'`.  Two cartesian squares then
become pushout squares of rings (`isPushout_appLE_of_isPullback_affineOpens`):

* the one over `S`, which makes `Γ(Y', U')` the tensor product `Γ(Y, U) ⊗_{Γ(S, V)} Γ(S', W)`, so
  that Stacks tag 0CEP (`Koszul.quasiRegular_and_h1Regular_baseChange_of_quotient_flat`) carries
  `s` to a quasi-regular family there — the flatness of `Γ(Y, U)/(s)` over `Γ(S, V)` that 0CEP
  asks for being flatness of `Γ(Z, j⁻¹U)`, since the two agree by
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ker_app_eq_span_range`;
* the one over `Y`, whose leg `Γ(Y, U) ⟶ Γ(Z, j⁻¹U)` is surjective, so that
  `Stacks.Flatness.ker_inl_of_isPushout` computes the kernel of `j'.app U'` as the ideal generated
  by the image of `s`.

Those two facts are exactly a quasi-regular generating family for the defining ideal of `j'` on
`U'`, once the kernel computation is turned back into a statement about the ideal sheaf by
`isGeneratedByOn_definingIdealOfHom_of_ker_app_eq_span`.

Only the quasi-regular half of Stacks tag 063R is proved here.  The `H₁`-regular half is
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.isH1RegularImmersion_baseChange_of_flat`, in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularImmersion.H1BaseChange`:  it runs on the same two pushout
squares and on the `H₁` half of
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.isQuasiRegular_and_isH1Regular_of_isPushout_of_ker_eq_span` below, but
reads `H₁`-regularity off affine opens through
`AlgebraicGeometry.isH1RegularIdealSheaf_iff_kerGeneratedBy`, which is proved downstream of this
file.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Lemma 31.22.1 (Tag 063R)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/063R)
* [Stacks Project, Lemma 31.21.2 (Tag 063J)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/063J)
* [Stacks Project, Lemma 31.20.2 (Tag 063G)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/063G)
* [Stacks Project, Lemma 15.84.4 (Tag 0CEP)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CEP)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite TopologicalSpace
open AlgebraicGeometry RingTheory.Sequence
